To install Zeek, you can use official binary packages, package managers, or build from source. The easiest and most common way to install the current Long Term Support (LTS) release of Zeek on Ubuntu 24.04 is via the official OpenSUSE Build Service (OBS) repository. [1] (https://docs.zeek.org/en/v9.0.0/install.html)

1. Install via Official Repository (Ubuntu 24.04)

Run the following commands in your terminal to add the repository, import the GPG key, and install the latest Zeek 9.0 LTS line: [1] (https://zeek.org/get-zeek/), [2] (https://docs.zeek.org/en/v9.0.0/install.html)
bash
# Add the official Zeek repository
echo 'deb https://download.opensuse.org/repositories/security:/zeek/xUbuntu_24.04/ /' | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/security:zeek.list

# Import the repository GPG key
curl -fsSL https://download.opensuse.org/repositories/security:zeek/xUbuntu_24.04/Release.key | gpg --dearmor | sudo tee /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/security_zeek.gpg > /dev/null

# Update your package list and install Zeek
sudo apt update
sudo apt install zeek-9.0
Use code with caution.
(Note: If you are prompted about a mail server configuration during installation, selecting "Local only" is usually sufficient for a standard setup). [1] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A69WwoGg0WU), [2] (https://www.howtoforge.com/how-to-install-zeek-network-security-monitoring-tool-on-ubuntu-22-04/)

2. Alternative Operating Systems

If you are not using Ubuntu, you can install Zeek using your system's package manager:

Operating System / Environment	Installation Command
macOS	brew install zeek
FreeBSD	sudo pkg install -y zeek
OpenBSD	doas pkg_add zeek
Docker	docker pull zeek/zeek


3. Post-Installation Setup (Linux)

Once installed, Zeek's binaries live in /opt/zeek/bin. Follow these steps to complete the environment setup: [1] (https://docs.zeek.org/en/v9.0.0/install.html)
1. Add Zeek to your System PATH:bash
echo "export PATH=\$PATH:/opt/zeek/bin" >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc
Use code with caution.
2. Verify the Installation:bash
zeek --version
Use code with caution.
3. Configure your Network Interface:
Open the node configuration file:bash
sudo nano /opt/zeek/etc/node.cfg
Use code with caution.
Find the line interface=eth0 (or similar) and change it to match your active sniffing interface (e.g., enp0s3 or eth0). You can find your active interfaces by running ip link.
4. Deploy and Start Zeek: [1] (https://rahulcyberx.medium.com/how-to-install-zeek-on-linux-cybersecurity-homelab-5-06ca91765fde)
bash
sudo zeekctl deploy
sudo zeekctl status
Use code with caution.
For advanced deployments or alternative builds, you can refer to the official Book of Zeek Installation Guide or download direct tarballs from the Get Zeek Portal. [1] (https://docs.zeek.org/en/v9.0.0/install.html), [2] (https://zeek.org/get-zeek/)
